<section>
    <p class="eyebrow">Step 1</p>
    <h3>Register the PHPUnit extension</h3>
    <pre><code class="language-xml" data-trim data-line-numbers="1-7|3|4-5">
&lt;!-- phpunit.dist.xml --&gt;
&lt;extensions&gt;
    &lt;bootstrap class="Symfony\Bridge\PhpUnit\SymfonyExtension"&gt;
        &lt;!-- optional: all recordings in a single directory --&gt;
        &lt;parameter name="http-recorder-directory" value="tests/records"/&gt;
    &lt;/bootstrap&gt;
&lt;/extensions&gt;
    </code></pre>
    <p class="subtitle" style="font-size: 0.6em;">
        Without the parameter, each <code>.har</code> file lives next to its test.
        With it, the tree follows the namespace: <code>tests/records/App/Tests/FooTest/testBar.har</code>
    </p>
    <aside class="notes">
        <p>Step one: in your phpunit.dist.xml, you register the extension of the PHPUnit Bridge.</p>
        <p>[click] It's the SymfonyExtension. It links your tests to the recorder: it knows which test is running, and therefore which file to use. Many projects already have it for ClockMock or DnsMock.</p>
        <p>[click] And there's an optional parameter, http-recorder-directory. Without it, each .har file lives next to its test. With it, all the recordings go into a single directory, and the tree follows the namespace: tests/records/App/Tests/FooTest/testBar.har.</p>
    </aside>
</section>
